{"type":"after","callId":"call@307","endTime":51024.667,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/$GSET and $PSET — game and player settings\n    \n\n and  — game and player settings\nThe two frames that set on-gun rules and the player's pools, identity and voice pack\n✅bench🔍appLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\n — validated against the captured \n\n\n#\nField\nCaptured\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n1\nfriendlyFire\n0 / 1\nFirmware-enforced, both directions. 0 blocks same-team damage and heals from enemies; 1 opens the gate. Replicated 2× with alternating values plus control.\n✅bench\n\n\n2\noutdoorMode\n0\nAPK field name; not exercised on the bench.\n🔍app\n\n\n3\ngunLaserRegion\n1\nAPK field name; not exercised on the bench.\n🔍app\n\n\n4\nautoAmbientLight\n0\nAPK field name; not exercised on the bench.\n🔍app\n\n\n5\ngyroscope\n1\nAPK field name; not exercised on the bench.\n🔍app\n\n\n6\nsecondaryBluetoothWeapons\n0\nAPK field name; not exercised on the bench.\n🔍app\n\n\n7\ncriticalShotModifier\n50\nAPK field name. Not score-to-win (byte-identical across captures with different win conditions).\n🔍app ✅bench\n\n\n8\ngameMods\n1\nAPK field name; not exercised on the bench.\n🔍app\n\n\nSource: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (GSET), protocol/brx-protocol.md §3, §7n; docs/experiment-log.md (FF enforcement table)\nThere is no respawn, time, lives or score token.Three captures at respawn 5/15/30 s and different clocks produced byte-identical  and , and the 8-field map from the app metadata contains none of them. Those live in the host. Stop looking.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7n\n — sample \n\n\ntok\nField\nSample\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n1\nplayer id\n6\n0-based, 0–63 (6 bits) — the app's UI shows 1–64 and writes id−1 (app 7 → wire 6, app 64 → 63, an out-of-range 69 clamps to 63). Ends up in every IR shot's P field and comes back as  token 3 on whoever you hit.\n✅bench\n\n\n2\n—\n0\n0 in every capture; 0/1/7 gave byte-identical behaviour. Inert.\n✅bench\n\n\n3\nHP\n45\nStarting/max HP. Echoed as  token 1 after .\n✅bench\n\n\n4\narmor\n70\nArmor pool ( token 2,  token 2).\n✅bench\n\n\n5\nshield\n70\nShield maximum. The pool starts at 0 and only fills via an IR  grant function — it is not BLE-writable as a value.\n✅bench\n\n\n6\n—\n50\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n7\n(empty)\n—\n\n—\n\n\n8+\npositional voice pack\nH44 JAD V33 V3I V3C V3G V3E V37 H06 H55 H13 H21 H02 U15 W71 A10\nSixteen sound ids on the wire. The app's metadata declares these voice-pack fields: deathAlarm, stealthDeathScream, musicMixOnDeath, deathScream, battleRespawnCry, meleeGrunt, shortPain, longPain, painRelief, missShothit, hitHp, hitArrmor, hitShield, hitCrit, emptyUnboundButtonSound, ammoOrGearPickUp, energyShieldLoop. Which wire slot carries which name: — (unknown).\n🔍app\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §3, §7e, §7p, §7r; protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (PSET); mcp/brx_mcp/gameconfig.py; docs/unknowns.md (A10b′, P3)\nNumbering a fleet is one token.Give every gun a distinct  token 1 at arm time and per-player kill attribution is BLE-native — no cable, no IR receiver. Show operators 1-based ids; write .Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7p, §7q\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@307"}
